INSERT INTO `module_contents` VALUES
(1,'F1.1','[\"Use Google Gemini responsibly inside the @hwhschools.org Workspace for gemini foundations.\",\"Apply the aggregated-only FERPA posture that matches the HWHS scorecard on every AI-assisted artifact.\"]','A Helena West Helena Schools educator wants to start using Google Gemini this week but is unsure how to do it in a way that respects the scorecard\'s FERPA posture and moves at least one of the three WIGs. Foundations gives every HWHS role a shared floor before the Teaching, Learning, and Systems strands begin.','Google Gemini is a generative AI tool available to every @hwhschools.org account inside Google Workspace. It is powerful at drafting, summarizing, and reformatting; it is unreliable at facts it wasn\'t trained on, standards codes, and anything requiring current student data. The HWHS posture treats Gemini as a first-draft engine with a human educator as the final signer — never the other way around.','Foundations is the WIG-aligned floor: WIG 1 (Customer Service) needs staff who can draft 24-hour responses fast, WIG 2 (PLC Fidelity) needs CTM leads who can produce an agenda by Monday 5 pm, and WIG 3 (ATLAS Achievement) needs teachers who can generate CFA drafts aligned to the standards Central High and J.F. Wahl are teaching.','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f0f4ff,#e8f0fe);border:1px solid #c3d9f7;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">📘 HWHS Research + Framework Anchor</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard treats every metric as aggregated %/n and never holds student-level data. Foundations installs the same discipline for AI use.</p><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;margin-top:0.75rem;\">This module draws on Mandinach &amp; Jackson\'s (2012) five-step data-literacy framework — identify problems, use data, transform data into information, transform information into decisions, evaluate outcomes — and pairs it with the Solution Tree PLC continuum and the DuFour 4 Questions that Helena West Helena Schools uses on CTM Wednesdays. Gemini accelerates the middle steps; the first and last remain a human educator\'s job.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef3c7,#fde68a);border:1px solid #f59e0b;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#92400e;\">🎯 WIG Tie-In</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Foundations serves all three WIGs at once by installing the shared vocabulary — prompting, editing, FERPA — that every downstream module assumes.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ecfdf5,#d1fae5);border:1px solid #10b981;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#065f46;\">✨ Gemini Move to Practice</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Practice how generative AI actually works and where it makes things up inside a Google Doc this week. Bring the artifact to your next CTM Wednesday and ask one teammate to red-team it.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef2f2,#fee2e2);border:1px solid #ef4444;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#991b1b;\">🔒 FERPA Discipline</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Foundations is where the FERPA muscle gets built. The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard is aggregated %/n only, and this platform follows the same posture. Never paste student names, IEP language, or raw scores into Gemini or any AI tool.</p></div>','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #d1d5db;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">🧑‍🏫 Facilitator Note (HWHS Context)</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Run this Foundations module before opening any Teaching or Systems strand module. It\'s the difference between staff using Gemini casually and staff using it the HWHS way. Use CTM Wednesday time or a Cougar Elevate planning window to run this module with your team. Encourage participants to bring an artifact from their real workload — a CTM agenda, a DFA rollup, an IRP/MIP/HIT plan, a ParentSquare draft — and improve it live with Gemini instead of writing throwaway examples.</p></div>','2026-07-07 01:50:08','2026-07-07 01:50:08'),
(2,'F1.2','[\"Use Google Gemini responsibly inside the @hwhschools.org Workspace for workspace + gemini.\",\"Apply the aggregated-only FERPA posture that matches the HWHS scorecard on every AI-assisted artifact.\"]','A Helena West Helena Schools educator wants to start using Google Gemini this week but is unsure how to do it in a way that respects the scorecard\'s FERPA posture and moves at least one of the three WIGs. Foundations gives every HWHS role a shared floor before the Teaching, Learning, and Systems strands begin.','Google Gemini is a generative AI tool available to every @hwhschools.org account inside Google Workspace. It is powerful at drafting, summarizing, and reformatting; it is unreliable at facts it wasn\'t trained on, standards codes, and anything requiring current student data. The HWHS posture treats Gemini as a first-draft engine with a human educator as the final signer — never the other way around.','Foundations is the WIG-aligned floor: WIG 1 (Customer Service) needs staff who can draft 24-hour responses fast, WIG 2 (PLC Fidelity) needs CTM leads who can produce an agenda by Monday 5 pm, and WIG 3 (ATLAS Achievement) needs teachers who can generate CFA drafts aligned to the standards Central High and J.F. Wahl are teaching.','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f0f4ff,#e8f0fe);border:1px solid #c3d9f7;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">📘 HWHS Research + Framework Anchor</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard treats every metric as aggregated %/n and never holds student-level data. Foundations installs the same discipline for AI use.</p><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;margin-top:0.75rem;\">This module draws on Mandinach &amp; Jackson\'s (2012) five-step data-literacy framework — identify problems, use data, transform data into information, transform information into decisions, evaluate outcomes — and pairs it with the Solution Tree PLC continuum and the DuFour 4 Questions that Helena West Helena Schools uses on CTM Wednesdays. Gemini accelerates the middle steps; the first and last remain a human educator\'s job.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef3c7,#fde68a);border:1px solid #f59e0b;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#92400e;\">🎯 WIG Tie-In</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Foundations serves all three WIGs at once by installing the shared vocabulary — prompting, editing, FERPA — that every downstream module assumes.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ecfdf5,#d1fae5);border:1px solid #10b981;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#065f46;\">✨ Gemini Move to Practice</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Practice using Gemini inside Docs, Sheets, Slides, and Gmail as an HWHS staff member inside a Google Doc this week. Bring the artifact to your next CTM Wednesday and ask one teammate to red-team it.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef2f2,#fee2e2);border:1px solid #ef4444;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#991b1b;\">🔒 FERPA Discipline</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Foundations is where the FERPA muscle gets built. The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard is aggregated %/n only, and this platform follows the same posture. Never paste student names, IEP language, or raw scores into Gemini or any AI tool.</p></div>','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #d1d5db;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">🧑‍🏫 Facilitator Note (HWHS Context)</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Run this Foundations module before opening any Teaching or Systems strand module. It\'s the difference between staff using Gemini casually and staff using it the HWHS way. Use CTM Wednesday time or a Cougar Elevate planning window to run this module with your team. Encourage participants to bring an artifact from their real workload — a CTM agenda, a DFA rollup, an IRP/MIP/HIT plan, a ParentSquare draft — and improve it live with Gemini instead of writing throwaway examples.</p></div>','2026-07-07 01:50:09','2026-07-07 01:50:09'),
(3,'F1.3','[\"Use Google Gemini responsibly inside the @hwhschools.org Workspace for wig orientation.\",\"Apply the aggregated-only FERPA posture that matches the HWHS scorecard on every AI-assisted artifact.\"]','A Helena West Helena Schools educator wants to start using Google Gemini this week but is unsure how to do it in a way that respects the scorecard\'s FERPA posture and moves at least one of the three WIGs. Foundations gives every HWHS role a shared floor before the Teaching, Learning, and Systems strands begin.','Google Gemini is a generative AI tool available to every @hwhschools.org account inside Google Workspace. It is powerful at drafting, summarizing, and reformatting; it is unreliable at facts it wasn\'t trained on, standards codes, and anything requiring current student data. The HWHS posture treats Gemini as a first-draft engine with a human educator as the final signer — never the other way around.','Foundations is the WIG-aligned floor: WIG 1 (Customer Service) needs staff who can draft 24-hour responses fast, WIG 2 (PLC Fidelity) needs CTM leads who can produce an agenda by Monday 5 pm, and WIG 3 (ATLAS Achievement) needs teachers who can generate CFA drafts aligned to the standards Central High and J.F. Wahl are teaching.','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f0f4ff,#e8f0fe);border:1px solid #c3d9f7;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">📘 HWHS Research + Framework Anchor</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard treats every metric as aggregated %/n and never holds student-level data. Foundations installs the same discipline for AI use.</p><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;margin-top:0.75rem;\">This module draws on Mandinach &amp; Jackson\'s (2012) five-step data-literacy framework — identify problems, use data, transform data into information, transform information into decisions, evaluate outcomes — and pairs it with the Solution Tree PLC continuum and the DuFour 4 Questions that Helena West Helena Schools uses on CTM Wednesdays. Gemini accelerates the middle steps; the first and last remain a human educator\'s job.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef3c7,#fde68a);border:1px solid #f59e0b;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#92400e;\">🎯 WIG Tie-In</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Foundations serves all three WIGs at once by installing the shared vocabulary — prompting, editing, FERPA — that every downstream module assumes.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ecfdf5,#d1fae5);border:1px solid #10b981;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#065f46;\">✨ Gemini Move to Practice</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Practice how the three WIGs (Customer Service, PLC Fidelity, ATLAS Achievement) shape every prompt you\'ll write inside a Google Doc this week. Bring the artifact to your next CTM Wednesday and ask one teammate to red-team it.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef2f2,#fee2e2);border:1px solid #ef4444;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#991b1b;\">🔒 FERPA Discipline</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Foundations is where the FERPA muscle gets built. The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard is aggregated %/n only, and this platform follows the same posture. Never paste student names, IEP language, or raw scores into Gemini or any AI tool.</p></div>','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #d1d5db;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">🧑‍🏫 Facilitator Note (HWHS Context)</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Run this Foundations module before opening any Teaching or Systems strand module. It\'s the difference between staff using Gemini casually and staff using it the HWHS way. Use CTM Wednesday time