on Tree PLC continuum and the DuFour 4 Questions that Helena West Helena Schools uses on CTM Wednesdays. Gemini accelerates the middle steps; the first and last remain a human educator\'s job.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef3c7,#fde68a);border:1px solid #f59e0b;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#92400e;\">🎯 WIG Tie-In</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Foundations serves all three WIGs at once by installing the shared vocabulary — prompting, editing, FERPA — that every downstream module assumes.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ecfdf5,#d1fae5);border:1px solid #10b981;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#065f46;\">✨ Gemini Move to Practice</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Practice situations where Gemini is the wrong tool — grading of record, IEP language, disciplinary decisions inside a Google Doc this week. Bring the artifact to your next CTM Wednesday and ask one teammate to red-team it.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef2f2,#fee2e2);border:1px solid #ef4444;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#991b1b;\">🔒 FERPA Discipline</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Foundations is where the FERPA muscle gets built. The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard is aggregated %/n only, and this platform follows the same posture. Never paste student names, IEP language, or raw scores into Gemini or any AI tool.</p></div>','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #d1d5db;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">🧑‍🏫 Facilitator Note (HWHS Context)</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Run this Foundations module before opening any Teaching or Systems strand module. It\'s the difference between staff using Gemini casually and staff using it the HWHS way. Use CTM Wednesday time or a Cougar Elevate planning window to run this module with your team. Encourage participants to bring an artifact from their real workload — a CTM agenda, a DFA rollup, an IRP/MIP/HIT plan, a ParentSquare draft — and improve it live with Gemini instead of writing throwaway examples.</p></div>','2026-07-07 01:50:09','2026-07-07 01:50:09'),
(8,'T1.1','[\"Explain how Google Gemini works and where it fails in an HWHS context.\",\"Apply the aggregated-%\\/n FERPA posture on every Gemini interaction (supports WIG 1, 2, and 3).\"]','Students at Central High and J.F. Wahl are using AI outside of school and staff have not yet aligned on how Gemini fits inside Helena West Helena Schools. Without a shared understanding of what Gemini can and cannot do, the tool ends up used inconsistently — sometimes brilliantly, sometimes in ways that put student data or academic integrity at risk.','Gemini is a generative model available inside every @hwhschools.org Google Workspace account. It excels at drafting, restating, and reformatting; it hallucinates on facts, misquotes standards, and cannot access current HWHS student data. Treating it as a first-draft engine with a human educator as the final signer is the HWHS default.','This is the shared floor before any deeper use. Without it, WIG 1 (comms) drifts into unchecked auto-replies, WIG 2 (PLC fidelity) drifts into copy-pasted agendas, and WIG 3 (ATLAS achievement) drifts into standards-misaligned CFAs. With it, Gemini becomes an accelerator on all three.','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f0f4ff,#e8f0fe);border:1px solid #c3d9f7;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">📘 HWHS Research + Framework Anchor</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">The HWHS scorecard\'s FERPA posture — aggregated %/n only — is the same posture required by every Gemini interaction on this platform. Solution Tree\'s PLC continuum names \'shared clarity on tools and terms\' as a marker of high-functioning teams.</p><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;margin-top:0.75rem;\">This module draws on Mandinach &amp; Jackson\'s (2012) five-step data-literacy framework — identify problems, use data, transform data into information, transform information into decisions, evaluate outcomes — and pairs it with the Solution Tree PLC continuum and the DuFour 4 Questions that Helena West Helena Schools uses on CTM Wednesdays. Gemini accelerates the middle steps; the first and last remain a human educator\'s job.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef3c7,#fde68a);border:1px solid #f59e0b;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#92400e;\">🎯 WIG Tie-In</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">This module protects all three WIGs by installing a shared understanding of what Gemini can and cannot do. Every downstream Teaching, Learning, and Systems module assumes staff have this floor.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ecfdf5,#d1fae5);border:1px solid #10b981;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#065f46;\">✨ Gemini Move to Practice</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Practice: open Gemini inside a Google Doc, ask it to unpack an Arkansas standard you\'re teaching next week, and red-team its response with a teammate at CTM Wednesday.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef2f2,#fee2e2);border:1px solid #ef4444;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#991b1b;\">🔒 FERPA Discipline</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Because Gemini hallucinates on specifics, staff need a disciplined check for standards codes and citations. The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard is aggregated %/n only, and this platform follows the same posture. Never paste student names, IEP language, or raw scores into Gemini or any AI tool.</p></div>','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #d1d5db;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">🧑‍🏫 Facilitator Note (HWHS Context)</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Run this module inside a CTM Wednesday block, not as a stand-alone PD. The point is to install the habit inside the workflow, not add a new workflow. Use CTM Wednesday time or a Cougar Elevate planning window to run this module with your team. Encourage participants to bring an artifact from their real workload — a CTM agenda, a DFA rollup, an IRP/MIP/HIT plan, a ParentSquare draft — and improve it live with Gemini instead of writing throwaway examples.</p></div>','2026-07-07 01:50:09','2026-07-07 01:50:09'),
(9,'T1.2','[\"Identify ethical, bias, and privacy risks when using Gemini in HWHS classrooms.\",\"Apply the HWHS aggregated-%\\/n posture to every Gemini interaction (supports WIG 1).\"]','A CHS teacher has been pasting student writing into Gemini for feedback. It reveals a privacy risk the HWHS scorecard is engineered to prevent — student-level data leaving the sanctioned aggregated posture. Cabinet needs staff aligned before this becomes a Board question.','Ethics, bias, and privacy in Gemini use are not abstract — they map directly to how HWHS handles data on the scorecard: aggregated %/n only, weighted by enrollment for rollups, no student-level PII in any AI tool.','This module lives at the intersection of WIG 1 (family trust) and the scorecard\'s FERPA posture — it protects the promise Cabinet has already made to families.','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f0f4ff,#e8f0fe);border:1px solid #c3d9f7;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">📘 HWHS Research + Framework Anchor</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">The scorecard\'s aggregated-%/n discipline was designed to survive audit. Extending that same discipline to Gemini use is the only way to keep the system safe as AI adoption grows.</p><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;margin-top:0.75rem;\">This module draws on Mandinach &amp; Jackson\'s (2012) five-step data-literacy framework — identify problems, use data, transform data into information, transform information into decisions, evaluate outcomes — and pairs it with the Solution Tree PLC continuum and the DuFour 4 Questions that Helena West Helena Schools uses on CTM Wednesdays. Gemini accelerates the middle steps; the first and last remain a human educator\'s job.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef3c7,#fde68a);border:1px solid #f59e0b;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#92400e;\">🎯 WIG Tie-In</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">This module is the safety layer for WIG 1 (Customer Service) — a single AI privacy incident would undermine the 24-hour response promise.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ecfdf5,#d1fae5);border:1px solid #10b981;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#065f46;\">✨ Gemini Move to Practice</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Practice: red-team a colleague\'s Gemini prompt at CTM Wednesday, looking specifically for PII exposure and biased phrasing.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef2f2,#fee2e2);border:1px solid #ef4444;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#991b1b;\">🔒 FERPA Discipline</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Any prompt that names a student, a family, or a raw score is out of policy — no exceptions. The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard is aggregated %/n only, and this platform follows the same posture. Never paste student names, IEP language, or raw scores into Gemini or any AI tool.</p></div>','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #d1d5db;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">🧑‍🏫 Facilitator Note (HWHS Context)</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">This one is best run twice: once with staff, once with a Board-facing summary for Cabinet. Use CTM Wednesday time or a Cougar Elevate planning window to run this module with your team. Encourage participants to bring an artifact from their real workload — a CTM agenda, a DFA rollup, an IRP/MIP/HIT plan, a ParentSquare draft — and improve it live with Gemini instead of writing throwaway examples.</p></div>','2026-07-07 01:50:09','2026-07-07 01:50:09'),
(10,'T1.3','[\"Establish HWHS-specific classroom norms for Gemini use.\",\"Align integrity expectations to the CHS Academic Playbook (supports WIG 2 and WIG 3).\"]','Students are turning in polished AI-assisted work with no visible thinking trail. Central High\'s Academic Playbook and J.F. Wahl\'s Literacy Plan both call for visible student thinking — HWHS needs shared norms that Gemini use does not erase.','Norms live in the Academic Playbook and the Literacy Plan. Extending them to AI use means naming what counts as \'student thinking\' when Gemini is in the loop.','This is a WIG 2 module: PLC teams need shared integrity language on Wednesday, and a WIG 3 module: CFAs need to keep predicting DFA performance even as AI use grows.','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f0f4ff,#e8f0fe);border:1px solid #c3d9f7;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">📘 HWHS Research + Framework Anchor</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">HWHS\'s mission line — Learning today. LEADING tomorrow. — puts student ownership at the center. Norms are how we operationalize it in the AI era.</p><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;margin-top:0.75rem;\">This module draws on Mandinach &amp; Jackson\'s (2012) five-step data-literacy framework — identify problems, use data, transform data into information, transform information into decisions, evaluate outcomes — and pairs it with the Solution Tree PLC continuum and the DuFour 4 Questions that Helena West Helena Schools uses on CTM Wednesdays. Gemini accelerates the middle steps; the first and last remain a human educator\'s job.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef3c7,#fde68a);border:1px solid #f59e0b;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#92400e;\">🎯 WIG Tie-In</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Without shared norms, WIG 3 metrics stop being trustworthy — a CFA polished by Gemini no longer predicts DFA performance.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ecfdf5,#d1fae5);border:1px solid #10b981;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#065f46;\">✨ Gemini Move to Practice</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Practice: draft one classroom norm with your CTM this Wednesday and post it visibly.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef2f2,#fee2e2);border:1px solid #ef4444;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#991b1b;\">🔒 FERPA Discipline</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Never include a student\'s actual work verbatim in a Gemini prompt — describe the pattern in aggregate instead. The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard is aggregated %/n only, and this platform follows the same posture. Never paste student names, IEP language, or raw scores into Gemini or any AI tool.</p></div>','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #d1d5db;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">🧑‍🏫 Facilitator Note (HWHS Context)</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Have CTMs run this together, not solo — the norm is only real if the whole grade level shares it. Use CTM Wednesday time or a Cougar Elevate planning window to run this module with your team. Encourage participants to bring an artifact from their real workload — a CTM agenda, a DFA rollup, an IRP/MIP/HIT plan, a ParentSquare draft — and improve it live with Gemini instead of writing throwaway examples.</p></div>','2026-07-07 01:50:09','2026-07-07 01:50:09'),
(11,'T2.1','[\"Design a lesson aligned to an Arkansas standard using Gemini as a first-draft engine.\",\"Predict DFA performance from the lesson\'s CFA (supports WIG 3).\"]','A CHS Math teacher needs three parallel lessons for a topic that will appear on DFA 3. Planning time is short and the DFA blueprint is public — Gemini can accelerate the first draft if the prompt names the standard code, the grade band, and the DFA blueprint anchor.','Standards-aligned design is the WIG 3 engine. The DFA blueprint is the target; the CFA is the predictor; the daily lesson is the delivery mechanism. Gemini shortens the draft cycle so more time goes to the delivery.','Every hour saved on drafting is an hour reinvested in Tier 2/3 supports — which is what actually moves DFA numbers.','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f0f4ff,#e8f0fe);border:1px solid #c3d9f7;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">📘 HWHS Research + Framework Anchor</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Solution Tree\'s PLC framework treats standards-alignment as a Wednesday responsibility, not a solo-planning responsibility. Gemini lowers the drafting cost so more of Wednesday goes to alignment.</p><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;margin-top:0.75rem;\">This module draws on Mandinach &amp; Jackson\'s (2012) five-step data-literacy framework — identify problems, use data, transform data into information, transform information into decisions, evaluate outcomes — and pairs it with the Solution Tree PLC continuum and the DuFour 4 Questions that Helena West Helena Schools uses on CTM Wednesdays. Gemini accelerates the middle steps; the first and last remain a human educator\'s job.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef3c7,#fde68a);border:1px solid #f59e0b;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#92400e;\">🎯 WIG Tie-In</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">This module is the highest-leverage WIG 3 module in the whole Institute. A tighter draft cycle means more CFA iterations before DFA windows close.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ecfdf5,#d1fae5);border:1px solid #10b981;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#065f46;\">✨ Gemini Move to Practice</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Practice: draft one lesson with Gemini this week, cross-check the standard code by hand.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef2f2,#fee2e2);border:1px solid #ef4444;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#991b1b;\">🔒 FERPA Discipline</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Never paste a specific student\'s misconception into Gemini — describe the class-level pattern instead. The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard is aggregated %/n only, and this platform follows the same posture. Never paste student names, IEP language, or raw scores into Gemini or any AI tool.</p></div>','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #d1d5db;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">🧑‍🏫 Facilitator Note (HWHS Context)</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Best run at the standards-unpacking phase of a unit, not the day-of. Use CTM Wednesday time or a Cougar Elevate planning window to run this module with your team. Encourage participants to bring an artifact from their real workload — a CTM agenda, a DFA rollup, an IRP/MIP/HIT plan, a ParentSquare draft — and improve it live with Gemini instead of writing throwaway examples.</p></div>','2026-07-07 01:50:09','2026-07-07 01:50:09'),
(12,'T2.2','[\"Differentiate a lesson at 3 access points using Gemini.\",\"Sequence a unit so each CFA predicts progress toward the DFA blueprint (supports WIG 3).\"]','A J.F. Wahl 4th-grade teacher has a class with a 5-grade-level spread. The Literacy Plan calls for UDL-aligned differentiation but drafting three parallel versions of every lesson eats the whole planning block. Gemini can produce the drafts; the teacher edits and sequences.','Differentiation is where UDL, the Literacy Plan, and MTSS meet. Gemini generates the variations; the teacher owns the sequencing decision.','This is a WIG 3 module — differentiation is one of the highest-leverage lead measures for moving ATLAS proficiency.','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f0f4ff,#e8f0fe);border:1px solid #c3d9f7;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">📘 HWHS Research + Framework Anchor</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Mandinach & Jackson\'s data-literacy framework and the HWHS Literacy Plan both name differentiation as the point where data becomes decisions.</p><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;margin-top:0.75rem;\">This module draws on Mandinach &amp; Jackson\'s (2012) five-step data-literacy framework — identify problems, use data, transform data into information, transform information into decisions, evaluate outcomes — and pairs it with the Solution Tree PLC continuum and the DuFour 4 Questions that Helena West Helena Schools uses on CTM Wednesdays. Gemini accelerates the middle steps; the first and last remain a human educator\'s job.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef3c7,#fde68a);border:1px solid #f59e0b;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#92400e;\">🎯 WIG Tie-In</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Without differentiation, WIG 3 stalls at the class-average — the students at the tails never move.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ecfdf5,#d1fae5);border:1px solid #10b981;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#065f46;\">✨ Gemini Move to Practice</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Practice: pick one lesson this week, generate 3 access points, share with your CTM.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef2f2,#fee2e2);border:1px solid #ef4444;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#991b1b;\">🔒 FERPA Discipline</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Access points are pattern-level, not student-level — no PII. The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard is aggregated %/n only, and this platform follows the same posture. Never paste student names, IEP language, or raw scores into Gemini or any AI tool.</p></div>','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #d1d5db;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">🧑‍🏫 Facilitator Note (HWHS Context)</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Run at the unit-planning stage so CFAs can be planned in parallel. Use CTM Wednesday time or a Cougar Elevate planning window to run this module with your team. Encourage participants to bring an artifact from their real workload — a CTM agenda, a DFA rollup, an IRP/MIP/HIT plan, a ParentSquare draft — and improve it live with Gemini instead of writing throwaway examples.</p></div>','2026-07-07 01:50:09','2026-07-07 01:50:09'),
(13,'T2.3','[\"Draft family- and staff-facing communication with Gemini.\",\"Meet the 24-hour response promise on family communication (supports WIG 1).\"]','The front office is missing the 24-hour response promise on a subset of family inquiries. Gemini can draft warm, on-brand replies inside Gmail so responders spend their time confirming facts, not composing from scratch.','The 24-hour response promise is a WIG 1 lead measure. Gemini turns the composition step from a bottleneck into a checkpoint.','This is the most direct WIG 1 module in the whole Institute. Every minute of drafting time saved goes toward hitting the 24-hour promise.','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f0f4ff,#e8f0fe);border:1px solid #c3d9f7;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">📘 HWHS Research + Framework Anchor</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">The Franklin Covey 4DX framework HWHS uses names \'act on lead measures\' as Discipline 2. Response-time is the lead measure that predicts WIG 1\'s climate-survey lag.</p><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;margin-top:0.75rem;\">This module draws on Mandinach &amp; Jackson\'s (2012) five-step data-literacy framework — identify problems, use data, transform data into information, transform information into decisions, evaluate outcomes — and pairs it with the Solution Tree PLC continuum and the DuFour 4 Questions that Helena West Helena Schools uses on CTM Wednesdays. Gemini accelerates the middle steps; the first and last remain a human educator\'s job.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef3c7,#fde68a);border:1px solid #f59e0b;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#92400e;\">🎯 WIG Tie-In</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">The scorecard tracks WIG 1 partly through response-time medians. Gemini-drafted first responses move that number without cutting corners on warmth or accuracy.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ecfdf5,#d1fae5);border:1px solid #10b981;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#065f46;\">✨ Gemini Move to Practice</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Practice: use Gemini to draft one family reply today; edit, sign, send within 24 hours.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef2f2,#fee2e2);border:1px solid #ef4444;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#991b1b;\">🔒 FERPA Discipline</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Family inquiries may contain student names — remove them before pasting into Gemini. The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard is aggregated %/n only, and this platform follows the same posture. Never paste student names, IEP language, or raw scores into Gemini or any AI tool.</p></div>','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #d1d5db;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">🧑‍🏫 Facilitator Note (HWHS Context)</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Front-office and instructional staff should run this together to keep tone consistent. Use CTM Wednesday time or a Cougar Elevate planning window to run this module with your team. Encourage participants to bring an artifact from their real workload — a CTM agenda, a DFA rollup, an IRP/MIP/HIT plan, a ParentSquare draft — and improve it live with Gemini instead of writing throwaway examples.</p></div>','2026-07-07 01:50:09','2026-07-07 01:50:09'),
(14,'T3.1','[\"Design CFAs whose results predict DFA performance.\",\"Anchor each CFA to the DFA blueprint and an Arkansas standard (supports WIG 3).\"]','DFA 2 is 4 weeks away and CTMs need CFAs that actually predict — not just check completion. Gemini can draft blueprint-anchored CFAs; the CTM edits and pilots them.','CFAs are the WIG 3 lead measure that predicts the DFA lag. The CTM Wednesday cadence and the 4-element fidelity rubric make the whole system testable.','This module is the mechanical heart of WIG 3.','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f0f4ff,#e8f0fe);border:1px solid #c3d9f7;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">📘 HWHS Research + Framework Anchor</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Solution Tree and Franklin Covey both name lead-measure discipline as the difference between hoping and knowing. CFA design is where hope becomes evidence.</p><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;margin-top:0.75rem;\">This module draws on Mandinach &amp; Jackson\'s (2012) five-step data-literacy framework — identify problems, use data, transform data into information, transform information into decisions, evaluate outcomes — and pairs it with the Solution Tree PLC continuum and the DuFour 4 Questions that Helena West Helena Schools uses on CTM Wednesdays. Gemini accelerates the middle steps; the first and last remain a human educator\'s job.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef3c7,#fde68a);border:1px solid #f59e0b;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#92400e;\">🎯 WIG Tie-In</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Every minute a CTM saves on CFA drafting is a minute reinvested in Tier 2/3 supports. That reinvestment is what moves DFA numbers.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ecfdf5,#d1fae5);border:1px solid #10b981;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#065f46;\">✨ Gemini Move to Practice</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Practice: draft this week\'s CFA with Gemini using the DFA blueprint as the anchor.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef2f2,#fee2e2);border:1px solid #ef4444;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#991b1b;\">🔒 FERPA Discipline</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Never paste last week\'s specific student responses into Gemini — describe the pattern. The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard is aggregated %/n only, and this platform follows the same posture. Never paste student names, IEP language, or raw scores into Gemini or any AI tool.</p></div>','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #d1d5db;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">🧑‍🏫 Facilitator Note (HWHS Context)</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Run at the top of every CTM Wednesday for the next 4 weeks. Use CTM Wednesday time or a Cougar Elevate planning window to run this module with your team. Encourage participants to bring an artifact from their real workload — a CTM agenda, a DFA rollup, an IRP/MIP/HIT plan, a ParentSquare draft — and improve it live with Gemini instead of writing throwaway examples.</p></div>','2026-07-07 01:50:09','2026-07-07 01:50:09'),
(15,'T3.2','[\"Design a reteach cycle grounded in CFA data.\",\"Move class-level %\\/n toward the DFA target (supports WIG 3).\"]','CFA 3 landed and the class-level %/n missed the DFA blueprint target. The CTM needs a reteach cycle by Monday — Gemini can draft the sequence; the teacher owns the delivery.','Reteach is the fastest lead-measure lever for WIG 3. It closes the loop between CFA data and DFA readiness.','This is a pure WIG 3 module — no reteach means no ATLAS movement.','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f0f4ff,#e8f0fe);border:1px solid #c3d9f7;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">📘 HWHS Research + Framework Anchor</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Bryk et al.\'s improvement science treats the reteach cycle as a mini PDSA loop. Gemini accelerates the P — plan — so the D-S-A can move faster.</p><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;margin-top:0.75rem;\">This module draws on Mandinach &amp; Jackson\'s (2012) five-step data-literacy framework — identify problems, use data, transform data into information, transform information into decisions, evaluate outcomes — and pairs it with the Solution Tree PLC continuum and the DuFour 4 Questions that Helena West Helena Schools uses on CTM Wednesdays. Gemini accelerates the middle steps; the first and last remain a human educator\'s job.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef3c7,#fde68a);border:1px solid #f59e0b;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#92400e;\">🎯 WIG Tie-In</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">The scorecard\'s rose/sky/amber colors show reteach urgency at a glance. This module is how CTMs respond when they see amber.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ecfdf5,#d1fae5);border:1px solid #10b981;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#065f46;\">✨ Gemini Move to Practice</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Practice: draft one reteach cycle this week from CFA class-level data.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef2f2,#fee2e2);border:1px solid #ef4444;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#991b1b;\">🔒 FERPA Discipline</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">CFA data goes in as aggregated %/n only — no student names. The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard is aggregated %/n only, and this platform follows the same posture. Never paste student names, IEP language, or raw scores into Gemini or any AI tool.</p></div>','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #d1d5db;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">🧑‍🏫 Facilitator Note (HWHS Context)</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Best run in the last 10 minutes of a CTM Wednesday, immediately after CFA review. Use CTM Wednesday time or a Cougar Elevate planning window to run this module with your team. Encourage participants to bring an artifact from their real workload — a CTM agenda, a DFA rollup, an IRP/MIP/HIT plan, a ParentSquare draft — and improve it live with Gemini instead of writing throwaway examples.</p></div>','2026-07-07 01:50:09','2026-07-07 01:50:09'),
(16,'T3.3','[\"Facilitate a CTM using Gemini as a drafting layer.\",\"Meet all four elements of the fidelity rubric (supports WIG 2).\"]','CTM Wednesdays are the machinery of PLC fidelity, but agenda drafting, protocol design, and Tier 2/3 closure eat the Monday-5-pm-agenda deadline. Gemini can carry the drafting load so CTM leads spend their time on facilitation.','The 4-element fidelity rubric is the WIG 2 lead measure. Gemini shortens the agenda-drafting step so all four elements can be met consistently.','This is the WIG 2 backbone module.','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f0f4ff,#e8f0fe);border:1px solid #c3d9f7;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">📘 HWHS Research + Framework Anchor</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">The Solution Tree continuum names \'consistent, standards-focused Wednesday cadence\' as the hallmark of a Sustaining PLC.</p><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;margin-top:0.75rem;\">This module draws on Mandinach &amp; Jackson\'s (2012) five-step data-literacy framework — identify problems, use data, transform data into information, transform information into decisions, evaluate outcomes — and pairs it with the Solution Tree PLC continuum and the DuFour 4 Questions that Helena West Helena Schools uses on CTM Wednesdays. Gemini accelerates the middle steps; the first and last remain a human educator\'s job.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef3c7,#fde68a);border:1px solid #f59e0b;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#92400e;\">🎯 WIG Tie-In</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Every CTM that hits all 4 elements moves WIG 2\'s fidelity %/n toward 100%. Gemini takes the friction out of the deadline.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ecfdf5,#d1fae5);border:1px solid #10b981;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#065f46;\">✨ Gemini Move to Practice</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Practice: draft this Wednesday\'s CTM agenda in Gemini by Monday 3 pm, edit by Monday 5 pm.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef2f2,#fee2e2);border:1px solid #ef4444;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#991b1b;\">🔒 FERPA Discipline</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">CTM agendas may reference student patterns — never specific student names. The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard is aggregated %/n only, and this platform follows the same posture. Never paste student names, IEP language, or raw scores into Gemini or any AI tool.</p></div>','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #d1d5db;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">🧑‍🏫 Facilitator Note (HWHS Context)</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Run this module with all CTM leads at once so agenda quality converges. Use CTM Wednesday time or a Cougar Elevate planning window to run this module with your team. Encourage participants to bring an artifact from their real workload — a CTM agenda, a DFA rollup, an IRP/MIP/HIT plan, a ParentSquare draft — and improve it live with Gemini instead of writing throwaway examples.</p></div>','2026-07-07 01:50:09','2026-07-07 01:50:09'),
(17,'T3.4','[\"Design assessments that stay valid as AI use grows.\",\"Align to CHS Academic Playbook integrity language (supports WIG 2 and WIG 3).\"]','Take-home writing tasks are drifting toward Gemini-drafted-Gemini-checked cycles with no visible student thinking. HWHS needs assessments that make thinking visible even when AI is in the loop.','AI-inclusive assessment design is not about detection — it\'s about task architecture: in-class drafting, retrieval, sourcing, and defense.','This protects WIG 3 (CFAs stay predictive) and WIG 2 (integrity language stays shared).','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f0f4ff,#e8f0fe);border:1px solid #c3d9f7;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">📘 HWHS Research + Framework Anchor</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">HWHS\'s 91.67% graduation rate story is only as strong as the assessments behind it. AI-inclusive design keeps that story honest.</p><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;margin-top:0.75rem;\">This module draws on Mandinach &amp; Jackson\'s (2012) five-step data-literacy framework — identify problems, use data, transform data into information, transform information into decisions, evaluate outcomes — and pairs it with the Solution Tree PLC continuum and the DuFour 4 Questions that Helena West Helena Schools uses on CTM Wednesdays. Gemini accelerates the middle steps; the first and last remain a human educator\'s job.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef3c7,#fde68a);border:1px solid #f59e0b;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#92400e;\">🎯 WIG Tie-In</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">If assessments lose validity, WIG 3 measurement drifts and the whole scorecard becomes less trustworthy. This module is the countermeasure.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ecfdf5,#d1fae5);border:1px solid #10b981;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#065f46;\">✨ Gemini Move to Practice</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Practice: redesign one take-home task into an AI-inclusive in-class task this week.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef2f2,#fee2e2);border:1px solid #ef4444;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#991b1b;\">🔒 FERPA Discipline</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Assessment task designs never contain student names. The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard is aggregated %/n only, and this platform follows the same posture. Never paste student names, IEP language, or raw scores into Gemini or any AI tool.</p></div>','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #d1d5db;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">🧑‍🏫 Facilitator Note (HWHS Context)</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Best run cross-CTM so grade-level assessment design stays coherent. Use CTM Wednesday time or a Cougar Elevate planning window to run this module with your team. Encourage participants to bring an artifact from their real workload — a CTM agenda, a DFA rollup, an IRP/MIP/HIT plan, a ParentSquare draft — and improve it live with Gemini instead of writing throwaway examples.</p></div>','2026-07-07 01:50:09','2026-07-07 01:50:09'),
(18,'T4.1','[\"Integrate SEL practices with Gemini-drafted supports.\",\"Anchor to the PBIS Matrix and the CHS Academic Playbook (supports WIG 1).\"]','The PBIS Matrix names schoolwide behavior expectations, but classroom SEL routines vary. Gemini can draft consistent SEL scripts; teachers edit for their room; the coach checks for alignment with the Matrix.','SEL is a WIG 1 accelerator — better classroom climate feeds better family perception feeds the WIG 1 climate survey baseline.','This is a WIG 1 climate module. It also indirectly serves WIG 3 — students who feel seen are more likely to engage with retrieval and reteach cycles.','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f0f4ff,#e8f0fe);border:1px solid #c3d9f7;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">📘 HWHS Research + Framework Anchor</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">PBIS + SEL are two sides of the same schoolwide behavior architecture at HWHS.</p><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;margin-top:0.75rem;\">This module draws on Mandinach &amp; Jackson\'s (2012) five-step data-literacy framework — identify problems, use data, transform data into information, transform information into decisions, evaluate outcomes — and pairs it with the Solution Tree PLC continuum and the DuFour 4 Questions that Helena West Helena Schools uses on CTM Wednesdays. Gemini accelerates the middle steps; the first and last remain a human educator\'s job.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef3c7,#fde68a);border:1px solid #f59e0b;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#92400e;\">🎯 WIG Tie-In</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">The WIG 1 climate survey needs a real baseline in Year 1. Consistent SEL routines drive that baseline higher.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ecfdf5,#d1fae5);border:1px solid #10b981;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#065f46;\">✨ Gemini Move to Practice</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Practice: draft one SEL micro-routine this week; align to the PBIS Matrix; run it Monday.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef2f2,#fee2e2);border:1px solid #ef4444;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#991b1b;\">🔒 FERPA Discipline</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">SEL routines are pattern-level — never name a specific student\'s SEL history. The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard is aggregated %/n only, and this platform follows the same posture. Never paste student names, IEP language, or raw scores into Gemini or any AI tool.</p></div>','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #d1d5db;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">🧑‍🏫 Facilitator Note (HWHS Context)</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Run alongside the PBIS coach so alignment is real, not aspirational. Use CTM Wednesday time or a Cougar Elevate planning window to run this module with your team. Encourage participants to bring an artifact from their real workload — a CTM agenda, a DFA rollup, an IRP/MIP/HIT plan, a ParentSquare draft — and improve it live with Gemini instead of writing throwaway examples.</p></div>','2026-07-07 01:50:09','2026-07-07 01:50:09'),
(19,'T4.2','[\"Draft Tier II In-Class Interventions with Gemini.\",\"Align to the MTSS Behavior Plan (supports WIG 1 and WIG 2).\"]','Teachers know a Tier II In-Class Intervention is needed but drafting takes time. Gemini can produce a first draft anchored to the MTSS Behavior Plan; the teacher and SPED lead edit for the room.','MTSS intervention design is where WIG 1 (climate) and WIG 2 (fidelity) meet. Consistent Tier II drafting keeps intervention practice fidelity-aligned across CHS and JFW.','This module cuts drafting time so more Tier II energy goes to delivery.','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f0f4ff,#e8f0fe);border:1px solid #c3d9f7;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">📘 HWHS Research + Framework Anchor</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Restorative supports at HWHS are grounded in the MTSS Behavior Plan and the PBIS Matrix. Gemini serves that architecture — it does not replace it.</p><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;margin-top:0.75rem;\">This module draws on Mandinach &amp; Jackson\'s (2012) five-step data-literacy framework — identify problems, use data, transform data into information, transform information into decisions, evaluate outcomes — and pairs it with the Solution Tree PLC continuum and the DuFour 4 Questions that Helena West Helena Schools uses on CTM Wednesdays. Gemini accelerates the middle steps; the first and last remain a human educator\'s job.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef3c7,#fde68a);border:1px solid #f59e0b;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#92400e;\">🎯 WIG Tie-In</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">The scorecard measures the intervention density indirectly through CFA reteach cycles and PBIS incident trends. Faster drafting means higher density.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ecfdf5,#d1fae5);border:1px solid #10b981;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#065f46;\">✨ Gemini Move to Practice</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Practice: draft one Tier II intervention this week for a class-level pattern.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef2f2,#fee2e2);border:1px solid #ef4444;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#991b1b;\">🔒 FERPA Discipline</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Intervention drafts describe patterns — never specific students. The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard is aggregated %/n only, and this platform follows the same posture. Never paste student names, IEP language, or raw scores into Gemini or any AI tool.</p></div>','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #d1d5db;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">🧑‍🏫 Facilitator Note (HWHS Context)</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Best run with SPED and PBIS leads in the room. Use CTM Wednesday time or a Cougar Elevate planning window to run this module with your team. Encourage participants to bring an artifact from their real workload — a CTM agenda, a DFA rollup, an IRP/MIP/HIT plan, a ParentSquare draft — and improve it live with Gemini instead of writing throwaway examples.</p></div>','2026-07-07 01:50:09','2026-07-07 01:50:09'),
(20,'T4.3','[\"Design ethical safeguards for AI-adjacent behavioral supports.\",\"Preserve human oversight on every behavioral decision (supports WIG 1).\"]','AI can suggest patterns from behavioral trend data, but every consequential decision — referral, intervention, restorative plan — belongs to a human. HWHS needs an ethical safeguards frame that names that boundary clearly.','Behavioral monitoring at HWHS is aggregated %/n at the pattern level, not surveillance at the student level. The safeguards frame makes that posture explicit.','This is a WIG 1 trust module — families need to know HWHS uses AI safely on behavior data as well as academic data.','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f0f4ff,#e8f0fe);border:1px solid #c3d9f7;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">📘 HWHS Research + Framework Anchor</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">The 4DX framework HWHS uses at the New Orleans Teacher Leader Institute treats trust as a compounding asset. Safeguards protect the compound.</p><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;margin-top:0.75rem;\">This module draws on Mandinach &amp; Jackson\'s (2012) five-step data-literacy framework — identify problems, use data, transform data into information, transform information into decisions, evaluate outcomes — and pairs it with the Solution Tree PLC continuum and the DuFour 4 Questions that Helena West Helena Schools uses on CTM Wednesdays. Gemini accelerates the middle steps; the first and last remain a human educator\'s job.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef3c7,#fde68a);border:1px solid #f59e0b;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#92400e;\">🎯 WIG Tie-In</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">The WIG 1 climate survey baseline depends on family trust. Ethical safeguards on behavior data protect that trust.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ecfdf5,#d1fae5);border:1px solid #10b981;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#065f46;\">✨ Gemini Move to Practice</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Practice: draft a 1-page \'safeguards\' card for your team this week.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef2f2,#fee2e2);border:1px solid #ef4444;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#991b1b;\">🔒 FERPA Discipline</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Behavior data is pattern-level in every AI prompt — no names, no incidents. The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard is aggregated %/n only, and this platform follows the same posture. Never paste student names, IEP language, or raw scores into Gemini or any AI tool.</p></div>','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #d1d5db;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">🧑‍🏫 Facilitator Note (HWHS Context)</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Should be run after T4.2 so the practice and the safeguards land together. Use CTM Wednesday time or a Cougar Elevate planning window to run this module with your team. Encourage participants to bring an artifact from their real workload — a CTM agenda, a DFA rollup, an IRP/MIP/HIT plan, a ParentSquare draft — and improve it live with Gemini instead of writing throwaway examples.</p></div>','2026-07-07 01:50:09','2026-07-07 01:50:09'),
(21,'L1.1','[\"Teach HWHS students how large language models work and hallucinate.\",\"Anchor the lesson to the Academic Playbook (supports WIG 3).\"]','Students at CHS and JFW use AI at home but do not have a shared model of how it works. Without that model, they can\'t evaluate its output — which weakens every downstream assessment.','Teaching students how AI works is a WIG 3 lever: better student evaluators produce better student work, which produces more accurate CFA-to-DFA prediction.','This module is the L-strand entry point.','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f0f4ff,#e8f0fe);border:1px solid #c3d9f7;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">📘 HWHS Research + Framework Anchor</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">The Academic Playbook names \'evaluators of information\' as a graduate quality. Teaching how AI works operationalizes it.</p><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;margin-top:0.75rem;\">This module draws on Mandinach &amp; Jackson\'s (2012) five-step data-literacy framework — identify problems, use data, transform data into information, transform information into decisions, evaluate outcomes — and pairs it with the Solution Tree PLC continuum and the DuFour 4 Questions that Helena West Helena Schools uses on CTM Wednesdays. Gemini accelerates the middle steps; the first and last remain a human educator\'s job.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef3c7,#fde68a);border:1px solid #f59e0b;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#92400e;\">🎯 WIG Tie-In</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">The 91.67% graduation-rate story at CHS is only durable if graduates leave with AI literacy. This is where that literacy starts.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ecfdf5,#d1fae5);border:1px solid #10b981;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#065f46;\">✨ Gemini Move to Practice</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Practice: teach one AI-literacy micro-lesson this week; anchor to a current unit.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef2f2,#fee2e2);border:1px solid #ef4444;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#991b1b;\">🔒 FERPA Discipline</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Micro-lessons describe AI at a system level — never analyze a specific student\'s AI use. The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard is aggregated %/n only, and this platform follows the same posture. Never paste student names, IEP language, or raw scores into Gemini or any AI tool.</p></div>','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #d1d5db;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">🧑‍🏫 Facilitator Note (HWHS Context)</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Best delivered by grade-level CTMs together so language stays consistent. Use CTM Wednesday time or a Cougar Elevate planning window to run this module with your team. Encourage participants to bring an artifact from their real workload — a CTM agenda, a DFA rollup, an IRP/MIP/HIT plan, a ParentSquare draft — and improve it live with Gemini instead of writing throwaway examples.</p></div>','2026-07-07 01:50:09','2026-07-07 01:50:09'),
(22,'L1.2','[\"Design personalized pathways that respect the HWHS Literacy Plan.\",\"Keep each pathway anchored to Arkansas standards (supports WIG 3).\"]','Students need different pathways to the same standard. Gemini can draft the branching; the teacher decides which branch fits which pattern of learners.','Personalization at HWHS is standards-first: the standard is the north star, and Gemini generates the routes to it.','This is a WIG 3 module — personalization is a lead measure for ATLAS movement.','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f0f4ff,#e8f0fe);border:1px solid #c3d9f7;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">📘 HWHS Research + Framework Anchor</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">The Literacy Plan and the Academic Playbook both call for pathways that end at the same standard even when they start at different places.</p><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;margin-top:0.75rem;\">This module draws on Mandinach &amp; Jackson\'s (2012) five-step data-literacy framework — identify problems, use data, transform data into information, transform information into decisions, evaluate outcomes — and pairs it with the Solution Tree PLC continuum and the DuFour 4 Questions that Helena West Helena Schools uses on CTM Wednesdays. Gemini accelerates the middle steps; the first and last remain a human educator\'s job.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef3c7,#fde68a);border:1px solid #f59e0b;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#92400e;\">🎯 WIG Tie-In</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Personalization done well tightens CFA-to-DFA prediction. Done poorly, it fragments the class and weakens the whole cycle.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ecfdf5,#d1fae5);border:1px solid #10b981;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#065f46;\">✨ Gemini Move to Practice</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Practice: design a 2-branch pathway this week for one class pattern.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef2f2,#fee2e2);border:1px solid #ef4444;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#991b1b;\">🔒 FERPA Discipline</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Pathways describe patterns — never a single student\'s IEP. The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard is aggregated %/n only, and this platform follows the same posture. Never paste student names, IEP language, or raw scores into Gemini or any AI tool.</p></div>','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #d1d5db;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">🧑‍🏫 Facilitator Note (HWHS Context)</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Run at unit-planning time, not day-of. Use CTM Wednesday time or a Cougar Elevate planning window to run this module with your team. Encourage participants to bring an artifact from their real workload — a CTM agenda, a DFA rollup, an IRP/MIP/HIT plan, a ParentSquare draft — and improve it live with Gemini instead of writing throwaway examples.</p></div>','2026-07-07 01:50:09','2026-07-07 01:50:09'),
(23,'L1.3','[\"Draft accessibility supports that meet UDL and the MTSS Behavior Plan.\",\"Support Cougar Elevate access for every learner (supports WIG 1 and WIG 3).\"]','Cougar Elevate afterschool serves students across HWHS but access varies. Gemini can draft warm invitations, bilingual family notes, and UDL-aligned session plans so no student misses a pathway to mastery.','Access is both a WIG 1 (family perception) and WIG 3 (learning outcomes) lever. Gemini shortens the drafting cycle so more energy goes to the students who need it most.','This module ties SEL, UDL, and Cougar Elevate together.','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f0f4ff,#e8f0fe);border:1px solid #c3d9f7;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">📘 HWHS Research + Framework Anchor</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Equity of access is named explicitly in the HWHS mission — LEADING tomorrow means graduating leaders from every background.</p><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;margin-top:0.75rem;\">This module draws on Mandinach &amp; Jackson\'s (2012) five-step data-literacy framework — identify problems, use data, transform data into information, transform information into decisions, evaluate outcomes — and pairs it with the Solution Tree PLC continuum and the DuFour 4 Questions that Helena West Helena Schools uses on CTM Wednesdays. Gemini accelerates the middle steps; the first and last remain a human educator\'s job.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef3c7,#fde68a);border:1px solid #f59e0b;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#92400e;\">🎯 WIG Tie-In</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Cougar Elevate is one of the most direct WIG 3 accelerators HWHS runs. Access is the gate. This module widens the gate.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ecfdf5,#d1fae5);border:1px solid #10b981;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#065f46;\">✨ Gemini Move to Practice</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Practice: draft one bilingual Cougar Elevate invitation this week.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef2f2,#fee2e2);border:1px solid #ef4444;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#991b1b;\">🔒 FERPA Discipline</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Invitations never name specific students — audience is described by pattern. The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard is aggregated %/n only, and this platform follows the same posture. Never paste student names, IEP language, or raw scores into Gemini or any AI tool.</p></div>','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #d1d5db;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">🧑‍🏫 Facilitator Note (HWHS Context)</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Best run with SPED, support staff, and Cougar Elevate leads together. Use CTM Wednesday time or a Cougar Elevate planning window to run this module with your team. Encourage participants to bring an artifact from their real workload — a CTM agenda, a DFA rollup, an IRP/MIP/HIT plan, a ParentSquare draft — and improve it live with Gemini instead of writing throwaway examples.</p></div>','2026-07-07 01:50:09','2026-07-07 01:50:09'),
(24,'L2.1','[\"Teach HWHS students to evaluate Gemini output for accuracy and bias.\",\"Anchor to the Literacy Plan and the Academic Playbook (supports WIG 3).\"]','Students accept Gemini output as fact unless taught otherwise. Central High Social Science and ELA CTMs need shared moves for teaching evaluation as a core skill.','Evaluation is a WIG 3 lever — better evaluators produce better CFA responses.','This module is where AI literacy becomes ATLAS movement.','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f0f4ff,#e8f0fe);border:1px solid #c3d9f7;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">📘 HWHS Research + Framework Anchor</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Bryk et al.\'s improvement science treats evaluation as a Wednesday habit, not a one-time lesson. This module builds the habit.</p><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;margin-top:0.75rem;\">This module draws on Mandinach &amp; Jackson\'s (2012) five-step data-literacy framework — identify problems, use data, transform data into information, transform information into decisions, evaluate outcomes — and pairs it with the Solution Tree PLC continuum and the DuFour 4 Questions that Helena West Helena Schools uses on CTM Wednesdays. Gemini accelerates the middle steps; the first and last remain a human educator\'s job.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef3c7,#fde68a);border:1px solid #f59e0b;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#92400e;\">🎯 WIG Tie-In</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">The Literacy Plan names \'evaluate sources\' as a schoolwide priority. Extending it to AI sources is the natural next step.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ecfdf5,#d1fae5);border:1px solid #10b981;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#065f46;\">✨ Gemini Move to Practice</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Practice: teach one \'evaluate Gemini\' micro-lesson this week; anchor to a unit source.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef2f2,#fee2e2);border:1px solid #ef4444;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#991b1b;\">🔒 FERPA Discipline</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Evaluation tasks are pattern-level — no PII in any prompt. The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard is aggregated %/n only, and this platform follows the same posture. Never paste student names, IEP language, or raw scores into Gemini or any AI tool.</p></div>','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #d1d5db;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">🧑‍🏫 Facilitator Note (HWHS Context)</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Best run in ELA and Social Science CTMs together. Use CTM Wednesday time or a Cougar Elevate planning window to run this module with your team. Encourage participants to bring an artifact from their real workload — a CTM agenda, a DFA rollup, an IRP/MIP/HIT plan, a ParentSquare draft — and improve it live with Gemini instead of writing throwaway examples.</p></div>','2026-07-07 01:50:09','2026-07-07 01:50:09'),
(25,'L2.2','[\"Design creative-production tasks that stay valid as AI use grows.\",\"Anchor to the Academic Playbook (supports WIG 2 and WIG 3).\"]','Student creative work is drifting toward AI-generated output with no visible student voice. HWHS needs task designs where AI is an ingredient, not the author.','Creative production tasks in the AI era need architecture: in-class drafting, revision trails, defense.','This module protects WIG 3 (assessment validity) and WIG 2 (shared integrity language).','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f0f4ff,#e8f0fe);border:1px solid #c3d9f7;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">📘 HWHS Research + Framework Anchor</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">The Academic Playbook names \'produce, don\'t just consume\' as a Cougar Way principle.</p><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;margin-top:0.75rem;\">This module draws on Mandinach &amp; Jackson\'s (2012) five-step data-literacy framework — identify problems, use data, transform data into information, transform information into decisions, evaluate outcomes — and pairs it with the Solution Tree PLC continuum and the DuFour 4 Questions that Helena West Helena Schools uses on CTM Wednesdays. Gemini accelerates the middle steps; the first and last remain a human educator\'s job.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef3c7,#fde68a);border:1px solid #f59e0b;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#92400e;\">🎯 WIG Tie-In</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">The 91.67% graduation-rate story includes students who left HWHS as creators, not just consumers. This module keeps that story true.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ecfdf5,#d1fae5);border:1px solid #10b981;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#065f46;\">✨ Gemini Move to Practice</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Practice: redesign one creative task this week to have a visible revision trail.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef2f2,#fee2e2);border:1px solid #ef4444;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#991b1b;\">🔒 FERPA Discipline</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Creative task designs are pattern-level, never named to a specific student. The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard is aggregated %/n only, and this platform follows the same posture. Never paste student names, IEP language, or raw scores into Gemini or any AI tool.</p></div>','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #d1d5db;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">🧑‍🏫 Facilitator Note (HWHS Context)</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Best run alongside T3.4 — the two modules reinforce each other. Use CTM Wednesday time or a Cougar Elevate planning window to run this module with your team. Encourage participants to bring an artifact from their real workload — a CTM agenda, a DFA rollup, an IRP/MIP/HIT plan, a ParentSquare draft — and improve it live with Gemini instead of writing throwaway examples.</p></div>','2026-07-07 01:50:10','2026-07-07 01:50:10'),
(26,'L3.1','[\"Design retrieval-practice cycles supported by Gemini.\",\"Aim retrieval at the DFA blueprint (supports WIG 3).\"]','Retrieval practice is one of the highest-leverage moves for ATLAS proficiency, but drafting daily retrieval questions eats teacher time. Gemini drafts; the teacher edits.','Retrieval is the WIG 3 lead measure between CFAs. Gemini shortens the drafting cost.','This is a WIG 3 workhorse module.','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f0f4ff,#e8f0fe);border:1px solid #c3d9f7;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">📘 HWHS Research + Framework Anchor</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">The learning-science research on retrieval (Roediger, Karpicke) is unambiguous. Gemini makes it operationally feasible at CTM cadence.</p><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;margin-top:0.75rem;\">This module draws on Mandinach &amp; Jackson\'s (2012) five-step data-literacy framework — identify problems, use data, transform data into information, transform information into decisions, evaluate outcomes — and pairs it with the Solution Tree PLC continuum and the DuFour 4 Questions that Helena West Helena Schools uses on CTM Wednesdays. Gemini accelerates the middle steps; the first and last remain a human educator\'s job.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef3c7,#fde68a);border:1px solid #f59e0b;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#92400e;\">🎯 WIG Tie-In</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Every additional day of retrieval that lands is a fractional %/n gain on the DFA. Small moves compound.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ecfdf5,#d1fae5);border:1px solid #10b981;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#065f46;\">✨ Gemini Move to Practice</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Practice: draft one week of retrieval questions this Sunday; run daily.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef2f2,#fee2e2);border:1px solid #ef4444;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#991b1b;\">🔒 FERPA Discipline</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Retrieval questions are unit-level, never student-level. The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard is aggregated %/n only, and this platform follows the same posture. Never paste student names, IEP language, or raw scores into Gemini or any AI tool.</p></div>','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #d1d5db;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">🧑‍🏫 Facilitator Note (HWHS Context)</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Best run in Math and Science CTMs first — highest retrieval leverage. Use CTM Wednesday time or a Cougar Elevate planning window to run this module with your team. Encourage participants to bring an artifact from their real workload — a CTM agenda, a DFA rollup, an IRP/MIP/HIT plan, a ParentSquare draft — and improve it live with Gemini instead of writing throwaway examples.</p></div>','2026-07-07 01:50:10','2026-07-07 01:50:10'),
(27,'L3.2','[\"Design reflection routines that raise student metacognition.\",\"Anchor to the CHS Academic Playbook (supports WIG 3).\"]','Metacognition predicts DFA performance more strongly than time-on-task. HWHS needs a shared reflection routine that lands at the end of every CFA cycle.','Reflection is a WIG 3 lever with long tails — the students who reflect consistently outperform peers of equal starting %/n.','This module ties the Academic Playbook\'s metacognition thread to a CTM Wednesday routine.','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f0f4ff,#e8f0fe);border:1px solid #c3d9f7;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">📘 HWHS Research + Framework Anchor</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">The graduate profile HWHS is co-authoring (Phase 3 of the OptimizED contract) puts metacognition at the center. This is where it starts.</p><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;margin-top:0.75rem;\">This module draws on Mandinach &amp; Jackson\'s (2012) five-step data-literacy framework — identify problems, use data, transform data into information, transform information into decisions, evaluate outcomes — and pairs it with the Solution Tree PLC continuum and the DuFour 4 Questions that Helena West Helena Schools uses on CTM Wednesdays. Gemini accelerates the middle steps; the first and last remain a human educator\'s job.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef3c7,#fde68a);border:1px solid #f59e0b;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#92400e;\">🎯 WIG Tie-In</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Reflection routines directly feed the DFA improvement narrative in the scorecard.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ecfdf5,#d1fae5);border:1px solid #10b981;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#065f46;\">✨ Gemini Move to Practice</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Practice: draft one reflection prompt after this week\'s CFA; run in every class.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef2f2,#fee2e2);border:1px solid #ef4444;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#991b1b;\">🔒 FERPA Discipline</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Reflection prompts are class-level, never student-level. The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard is aggregated %/n only, and this platform follows the same posture. Never paste student names, IEP language, or raw scores into Gemini or any AI tool.</p></div>','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #d1d5db;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">🧑‍🏫 Facilitator Note (HWHS Context)</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Best run with the Portrait of a Graduate work already underway. Use CTM Wednesday time or a Cougar Elevate planning window to run this module with your team. Encourage participants to bring an artifact from their real workload — a CTM agenda, a DFA rollup, an IRP/MIP/HIT plan, a ParentSquare draft — and improve it live with Gemini instead of writing throwaway examples.</p></div>','2026-07-07 01:50:10','2026-07-07 01:50:10'),
(28,'L3.3','[\"Design a mastery-tracking routine that raises student goal ownership.\",\"Align to Arkansas standards and the DFA blueprint (supports WIG 3).\"]','Students who own their mastery data outperform peers of equal starting %/n. HWHS needs a shared mastery-tracking routine that students can run themselves.','Mastery ownership is a compounding WIG 3 lever. It also feeds WIG 1 — engaged students become the story families tell.','This module is the closer for the Learning strand.','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f0f4ff,#e8f0fe);border:1px solid #c3d9f7;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">📘 HWHS Research + Framework Anchor</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">The Portrait of a Graduate work anchors goal-ownership as a Cougar Way skill.</p><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;margin-top:0.75rem;\">This module draws on Mandinach &amp; Jackson\'s (2012) five-step data-literacy framework — identify problems, use data, transform data into information, transform information into decisions, evaluate outcomes — and pairs it with the Solution Tree PLC continuum and the DuFour 4 Questions that Helena West Helena Schools uses on CTM Wednesdays. Gemini accelerates the middle steps; the first and last remain a human educator\'s job.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef3c7,#fde68a);border:1px solid #f59e0b;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#92400e;\">🎯 WIG Tie-In</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">The scorecard tracks aggregated mastery. Student-owned mastery tracking makes the aggregation trustworthy.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ecfdf5,#d1fae5);border:1px solid #10b981;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#065f46;\">✨ Gemini Move to Practice</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Practice: run a mastery-tracking pilot with one class this week.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef2f2,#fee2e2);border:1px solid #ef4444;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#991b1b;\">🔒 FERPA Discipline</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Mastery tracking is student-owned but school-aggregated — never paste tracker contents into any AI tool. The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard is aggregated %/n only, and this platform follows the same posture. Never paste student names, IEP language, or raw scores into Gemini or any AI tool.</p></div>','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #d1d5db;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">🧑‍🏫 Facilitator Note (HWHS Context)</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Best run in the last month of a DFA cycle. Use CTM Wednesday time or a Cougar Elevate planning window to run this module with your team. Encourage participants to bring an artifact from their real workload — a CTM agenda, a DFA rollup, an IRP/MIP/HIT plan, a ParentSquare draft — and improve it live with Gemini instead of writing throwaway examples.</p></div>','2026-07-07 01:50:10','2026-07-07 01:50:10'),
(29,'D1.1','[\"Analyze HWHS-level data using Gemini to surface actionable patterns.\",\"Anchor findings to the three WIGs and the scorecard rollup rules (supports all WIGs).\"]','Cabinet needs to move from data-rich to insight-rich fast. Gemini can accelerate the pattern-surfacing step; the human owns the interpretation and the response.','Needs assessment at HWHS is the front end of the scorecard\'s monthly rhythm. Gemini shortens the pattern-surfacing time so more of the meeting goes to decision-making.','This module ties directly to the scorecard\'s Cabinet surface.','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f0f4ff,#e8f0fe);border:1px solid #c3d9f7;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">📘 HWHS Research + Framework Anchor</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">The 4DX Focus discipline names \'the wildly important few\' as the point of the exercise. This module makes that discipline operational.</p><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;margin-top:0.75rem;\">This module draws on Mandinach &amp; Jackson\'s (2012) five-step data-literacy framework — identify problems, use data, transform data into information, transform information into decisions, evaluate outcomes — and pairs it with the Solution Tree PLC continuum and the DuFour 4 Questions that Helena West Helena Schools uses on CTM Wednesdays. Gemini accelerates the middle steps; the first and last remain a human educator\'s job.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef3c7,#fde68a);border:1px solid #f59e0b;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#92400e;\">🎯 WIG Tie-In</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">The scorecard was built to weight rollups by enrollment (n). Gemini-drafted needs assessments must honor that math, not simple-average across schools.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ecfdf5,#d1fae5);border:1px solid #10b981;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#065f46;\">✨ Gemini Move to Practice</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Practice: run a Gemini-assisted needs assessment on last month\'s scorecard this week.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef2f2,#fee2e2);border:1px solid #ef4444;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#991b1b;\">🔒 FERPA Discipline</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Data pasted into Gemini is aggregated %/n only. The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard is aggregated %/n only, and this platform follows the same posture. Never paste student names, IEP language, or raw scores into Gemini or any AI tool.</p></div>','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #d1d5db;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">🧑‍🏫 Facilitator Note (HWHS Context)</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Best run 3 days before the monthly Guiding Coalition meeting. Use CTM Wednesday time or a Cougar Elevate planning window to run this module with your team. Encourage participants to bring an artifact from their real workload — a CTM agenda, a DFA rollup, an IRP/MIP/HIT plan, a ParentSquare draft — and improve it live with Gemini instead of writing throwaway examples.</p></div>','2026-07-07 01:50:10','2026-07-07 01:50:10'),
(30,'D1.2','[\"Interpret the HWHS scorecard\'s rose\\/sky\\/amber signals with Gemini support.\",\"Draft narratives that match the scorecard\'s audience voices (supports all WIGs).\"]','The scorecard writes pre-coded narratives, but Cabinet occasionally needs a longer diagnostic. Gemini drafts; Cabinet edits into the Superintendent voice.','Scorecard interpretation is a Cabinet workflow. Gemini shortens the drafting cost of extending the pre-coded narratives when a metric needs deeper explanation.','This module protects the scorecard\'s audience discipline — same data, different voice for Cabinet, principals, Board, families.','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f0f4ff,#e8f0fe);border:1px solid #c3d9f7;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">📘 HWHS Research + Framework Anchor</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Franklin Covey\'s 4DX Compelling Scoreboard discipline names \'players know at a glance if they\'re winning.\' This module keeps that clarity as narratives grow.</p><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;margin-top:0.75rem;\">This module draws on Mandinach &amp; Jackson\'s (2012) five-step data-literacy framework — identify problems, use data, transform data into information, transform information into decisions, evaluate outcomes — and pairs it with the Solution Tree PLC continuum and the DuFour 4 Questions that Helena West Helena Schools uses on CTM Wednesdays. Gemini accelerates the middle steps; the first and last remain a human educator\'s job.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef3c7,#fde68a);border:1px solid #f59e0b;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#92400e;\">🎯 WIG Tie-In</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">The scorecard\'s audience-specific narratives are a WIG 1 asset. Gemini keeps voice consistent as more people draft.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ecfdf5,#d1fae5);border:1px solid #10b981;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#065f46;\">✨ Gemini Move to Practice</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Practice: extend one scorecard narrative in Cabinet voice this week.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef2f2,#fee2e2);border:1px solid #ef4444;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#991b1b;\">🔒 FERPA Discipline</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Extended narratives are aggregated %/n only. The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard is aggregated %/n only, and this platform follows the same posture. Never paste student names, IEP language, or raw scores into Gemini or any AI tool.</p></div>','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #d1d5db;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">🧑‍🏫 Facilitator Note (HWHS Context)</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Run monthly with the scorecard packet. Use CTM Wednesday time or a Cougar Elevate planning window to run this module with your team. Encourage participants to bring an artifact from their real workload — a CTM agenda, a DFA rollup, an IRP/MIP/HIT plan, a ParentSquare draft — and improve it live with Gemini instead of writing throwaway examples.</p></div>','2026-07-07 01:50:10','2026-07-07 01:50:10'),
(31,'D1.3','[\"Strengthen CTM Wednesday cadence with Gemini-drafted supports.\",\"Move the 4-element fidelity %\\/n toward 100% (supports WIG 2).\"]','PLC fidelity varies across the 15 HWHS CTMs. Gemini can draft consistent supports — agendas, protocols, closure templates — so fidelity converges without CTM leads burning out.','This is the WIG 2 backbone from a Systems perspective. Consistent supports at the system level unlock 4-element fidelity at the CTM level.','This module ties D1.3 to T3.3 as the two sides of PLC fidelity — one from the coach seat, one from the Cabinet seat.','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f0f4ff,#e8f0fe);border:1px solid #c3d9f7;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">📘 HWHS Research + Framework Anchor</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">The Solution Tree continuum names \'sustained cadence\' as the top rung. This module is the mechanism.</p><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;margin-top:0.75rem;\">This module draws on Mandinach &amp; Jackson\'s (2012) five-step data-literacy framework — identify problems, use data, transform data into information, transform information into decisions, evaluate outcomes — and pairs it with the Solution Tree PLC continuum and the DuFour 4 Questions that Helena West Helena Schools uses on CTM Wednesdays. Gemini accelerates the middle steps; the first and last remain a human educator\'s job.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef3c7,#fde68a);border:1px solid #f59e0b;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#92400e;\">🎯 WIG Tie-In</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">The WIG 2 rollup on the scorecard moves when CTM-level submissions come in consistently. Gemini-drafted supports remove friction from that cadence.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ecfdf5,#d1fae5);border:1px solid #10b981;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#065f46;\">✨ Gemini Move to Practice</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Practice: draft one CTM support this week; publish to all 15 CTMs.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef2f2,#fee2e2);border:1px solid #ef4444;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#991b1b;\">🔒 FERPA Discipline</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">CTM support materials are cadence-level, never CTM-member-specific. The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard is aggregated %/n only, and this platform follows the same posture. Never paste student names, IEP language, or raw scores into Gemini or any AI tool.</p></div>','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #d1d5db;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">🧑‍🏫 Facilitator Note (HWHS Context)</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Run on a rolling monthly cadence. Use CTM Wednesday time or a Cougar Elevate planning window to run this module with your team. Encourage participants to bring an artifact from their real workload — a CTM agenda, a DFA rollup, an IRP/MIP/HIT plan, a ParentSquare draft — and improve it live with Gemini instead of writing throwaway examples.</p></div>','2026-07-07 01:50:10','2026-07-07 01:50:10'),
(32,'D1.4','[\"Draft school improvement plan sections using Gemini.\",\"Anchor every section to a WIG and a scorecard metric (supports all WIGs).\"]','The CHS and JFW School Improvement Plans need to reflect the three WIGs cleanly. Gemini can draft the sections; the principal and Cabinet edit into HWHS voice.','School improvement planning at HWHS is scorecard-first. Gemini keeps drafts tight to the scorecard\'s WIG structure.','This is where system-level goals meet school-level execution.','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f0f4ff,#e8f0fe);border:1px solid #c3d9f7;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">📘 HWHS Research + Framework Anchor</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Franklin Covey\'s Cadence of Accountability discipline names quarterly reviews as the rhythm. School plans anchor to that rhythm at HWHS.</p><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;margin-top:0.75rem;\">This module draws on Mandinach &amp; Jackson\'s (2012) five-step data-literacy framework — identify problems, use data, transform data into information, transform information into decisions, evaluate outcomes — and pairs it with the Solution Tree PLC continuum and the DuFour 4 Questions that Helena West Helena Schools uses on CTM Wednesdays. Gemini accelerates the middle steps; the first and last remain a human educator\'s job.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef3c7,#fde68a);border:1px solid #f59e0b;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#92400e;\">🎯 WIG Tie-In</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">The scorecard rolls school-level metrics up to the district. School plans that align to the scorecard produce cleaner rollups.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ecfdf5,#d1fae5);border:1px solid #10b981;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#065f46;\">✨ Gemini Move to Practice</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Practice: draft one improvement plan section this week.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef2f2,#fee2e2);border:1px solid #ef4444;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#991b1b;\">🔒 FERPA Discipline</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Plan sections describe patterns, never individuals. The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard is aggregated %/n only, and this platform follows the same posture. Never paste student names, IEP language, or raw scores into Gemini or any AI tool.</p></div>','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #d1d5db;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">🧑‍🏫 Facilitator Note (HWHS Context)</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Best run at Cabinet + principal jointly. Use CTM Wednesday time or a Cougar Elevate planning window to run this module with your team. Encourage participants to bring an artifact from their real workload — a CTM agenda, a DFA rollup, an IRP/MIP/HIT plan, a ParentSquare draft — and improve it live with Gemini instead of writing throwaway examples.</p></div>','2026-07-07 01:50:10','2026-07-07 01:50:10'),
(33,'D2.1','[\"Draft the HWHS AI Acceptable Use Policy with Gemini.\",\"Ground the policy in the scorecard\'s FERPA posture (supports WIG 1).\"]','HWHS needs a public AI AUP that Cabinet, the Board, and families can all sign off on. Gemini drafts; Cabinet, legal, and Board edit.','The AUP is the WIG 1 policy foundation. It codifies the aggregated-only posture the scorecard already lives by.','This is the most consequential D2 module.','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f0f4ff,#e8f0fe);border:1px solid #c3d9f7;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">📘 HWHS Research + Framework Anchor</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Public districts moving fast on AI have gotten in trouble when policy trailed practice. HWHS reverses the order.</p><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;margin-top:0.75rem;\">This module draws on Mandinach &amp; Jackson\'s (2012) five-step data-literacy framework — identify problems, use data, transform data into information, transform information into decisions, evaluate outcomes — and pairs it with the Solution Tree PLC continuum and the DuFour 4 Questions that Helena West Helena Schools uses on CTM Wednesdays. Gemini accelerates the middle steps; the first and last remain a human educator\'s job.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef3c7,#fde68a);border:1px solid #f59e0b;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#92400e;\">🎯 WIG Tie-In</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">The scorecard is only as trustworthy as the policies behind it. This module writes the policy that makes the scorecard defensible at Board level.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ecfdf5,#d1fae5);border:1px solid #10b981;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#065f46;\">✨ Gemini Move to Practice</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Practice: draft the AUP skeleton this week; circulate at the next Cabinet meeting.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef2f2,#fee2e2);border:1px solid #ef4444;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#991b1b;\">🔒 FERPA Discipline</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Policy drafts do not need student data — they need policy patterns. The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard is aggregated %/n only, and this platform follows the same posture. Never paste student names, IEP language, or raw scores into Gemini or any AI tool.</p></div>','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #d1d5db;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">🧑‍🏫 Facilitator Note (HWHS Context)</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Cabinet + Board liaison should run this together. Use CTM Wednesday time or a Cougar Elevate planning window to run this module with your team. Encourage participants to bring an artifact from their real workload — a CTM agenda, a DFA rollup, an IRP/MIP/HIT plan, a ParentSquare draft — and improve it live with Gemini instead of writing throwaway examples.</p></div>','2026-07-07 01:50:10','2026-07-07 01:50:10'),
(34,'D2.2','[\"Draft family- and Board-facing AI communication with Gemini.\",\"Meet the 24-hour response promise (supports WIG 1).\"]','Families and the Board hear about AI from many sources. HWHS needs a single, consistent voice across ParentSquare, Apptegy Rooms, and Board packets.','This is the WIG 1 comms module for AI-adjacent messages.','The Franklin Covey Cadence of Accountability discipline names \'the same message at every altitude\' as a marker of a healthy system.','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f0f4ff,#e8f0fe);border:1px solid #c3d9f7;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">📘 HWHS Research + Framework Anchor</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">The 91.67% graduation-rate release and the Early Intervention exit release are the two current best examples of consistent HWHS voice. This module extends that pattern to AI.</p><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;margin-top:0.75rem;\">This module draws on Mandinach &amp; Jackson\'s (2012) five-step data-literacy framework — identify problems, use data, transform data into information, transform information into decisions, evaluate outcomes — and pairs it with the Solution Tree PLC continuum and the DuFour 4 Questions that Helena West Helena Schools uses on CTM Wednesdays. Gemini accelerates the middle steps; the first and last remain a human educator\'s job.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef3c7,#fde68a);border:1px solid #f59e0b;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#92400e;\">🎯 WIG Tie-In</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">The scorecard\'s community view is the ground floor. This module drafts the messages that sit on top of it.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ecfdf5,#d1fae5);border:1px solid #10b981;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#065f46;\">✨ Gemini Move to Practice</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Practice: draft one AI-adjacent family message this week.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef2f2,#fee2e2);border:1px solid #ef4444;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#991b1b;\">🔒 FERPA Discipline</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Family messages describe patterns and policies — never individual students. The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard is aggregated %/n only, and this platform follows the same posture. Never paste student names, IEP language, or raw scores into Gemini or any AI tool.</p></div>','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #d1d5db;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">🧑‍🏫 Facilitator Note (HWHS Context)</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Cabinet + communications lead + principal should run this together. Use CTM Wednesday time or a Cougar Elevate planning window to run this module with your team. Encourage participants to bring an artifact from their real workload — a CTM agenda, a DFA rollup, an IRP/MIP/HIT plan, a ParentSquare draft — and improve it live with Gemini instead of writing throwaway examples.</p></div>','2026-07-07 01:50:10','2026-07-07 01:50:10'),
(35,'D2.3','[\"Design HWHS professional growth pathways for AI capability.\",\"Anchor to the three WIGs and the CTM Wednesday cadence (supports WIG 2).\"]','Staff capability with Gemini varies. HWHS needs a growth pathway that meets people where they are and moves everyone toward the same shared floor by end of year.','This is the WIG 2 capacity module at the system level.','Every point of shared capability compounds — WIG 2 fidelity gets easier as more staff hit the shared floor.','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f0f4ff,#e8f0fe);border:1px solid #c3d9f7;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">📘 HWHS Research + Framework Anchor</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">The 4DX Focus discipline reminds us that spreading effort thin kills WIGs. The growth pathway concentrates energy at the WIGs.</p><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;margin-top:0.75rem;\">This module draws on Mandinach &amp; Jackson\'s (2012) five-step data-literacy framework — identify problems, use data, transform data into information, transform information into decisions, evaluate outcomes — and pairs it with the Solution Tree PLC continuum and the DuFour 4 Questions that Helena West Helena Schools uses on CTM Wednesdays. Gemini accelerates the middle steps; the first and last remain a human educator\'s job.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef3c7,#fde68a);border:1px solid #f59e0b;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#92400e;\">🎯 WIG Tie-In</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">The Solution Tree continuum names \'shared professional practice\' as a Sustaining marker.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#ecfdf5,#d1fae5);border:1px solid #10b981;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#065f46;\">✨ Gemini Move to Practice</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Practice: draft one growth pathway increment this week.</p></div><div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#fef2f2,#fee2e2);border:1px solid #ef4444;margin-top:1rem;\"><h3 style=\"color:#991b1b;\">🔒 FERPA Discipline</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Growth pathways are role-level, never person-level. The Helena West Helena Schools scorecard is aggregated %/n only, and this platform follows the same posture. Never paste student names, IEP language, or raw scores into Gemini or any AI tool.</p></div>','<div class=\"content-card\" style=\"background:#f9fafb;border:1px solid #d1d5db;\"><h3 style=\"color:#0B2E4F;\">🧑‍🏫 Facilitator Note (HWHS Context)</h3><p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;color:#374151;line-height:1.75;\">Best run at Cabinet + principal + coach together. Use CTM Wednesday time or a Cougar Elevate planning window to run this module with your team. Encourage participants to bring an artifact from their real workload — a CTM agenda, a DFA rollup, an IRP/MIP/HIT plan, a ParentSquare draft — and improve it live with Gemini instead of writing throwaway examples.</p></div>','2026-07-07 01:50:10','2026-07-07 01:50:10');
